## 10. Protect the free API quotas

Implement:

- maximum question length;
- maximum history length;
- maximum retrieved context;
- short output limit;
- request timeout;
- one controlled retry at most;
- exponential backoff for `429` and temporary `5xx` responses;
- circuit breaker after repeated provider failures;
- deterministic fallback;
- duplicate-submission prevention;
- sensible rate limiting;
- no automatic request on page load;
- no background AI summarization;
- no sending the full corpus;
- no AI calls for the timeline, checklist, pathways or meeting kit.

Do not automatically call both providers. Call Groq only if Gemini fails with an eligible temporary error.

Do not fall back for:

- invalid user input;
- safety rejection;
- unsupported request;
- insufficient verified context.

The timeline, maps, rule evaluation, checklist, calendar and meeting kit must continue working when quotas are exhausted.

## 11. Privacy changes

Adding optional runtime AI changes the current privacy claim.

Update the Privacy page and README so they accurately explain:

- deterministic evaluation stays in the browser;
- AI chat is optional;
- chat questions may be sent to the configured provider;
- only limited non-identifying context is transmitted;
- the application does not intentionally store conversation history;
- provider processing is governed by the provider’s policies;
- students should not enter legal identifiers;
- the app remains useful when AI is disabled.

Before the first AI-enhanced message, display a brief disclosure and require acknowledgement.

Add lightweight detection for likely:

- SEVIS IDs;
- passport numbers;
- A-numbers;
- receipt numbers;
- unusually long numeric identifiers.

When detected, do not send the message. Ask the student to remove the identifier.

Do not log complete student questions or profile dates in production logs.

## 12. Safety and insufficient information

For unsupported or high-risk questions, return approved responses.

Examples:

### Status determination

> Stay Valid cannot determine whether you are maintaining immigration status. Review the displayed dates and official sources, then confirm your circumstances with your DSO or a qualified immigration attorney.

### Insufficient evidence

> I could not find enough verified information in the current Stay Valid research corpus to answer that question. Please confirm it with your DSO and consult the linked official government sources.

### Out of scope

> Stay Valid currently focuses on educational preparation for F-1 students. It cannot answer this question reliably from its verified sources.

### Emergency or enforcement matter

Direct the student to their DSO and a qualified immigration attorney. Do not attempt to resolve urgent legal circumstances through AI.

